    candidate_certificate_route:
      "This candidate attacks the free branch-antisymmetric coordinate by testing the natural common-normalizer identity r_b=lambda*s_b. If s_-+s_+ is separated from zero, the aggregate equation R=r_-+r_+ gives lambda=R/(s_-+s_+) and t=R*(s_- - s_+)/(2*(s_-+s_+)). The packet computes those interval objects where division is allowed and keeps the common-normalizer law unproven. It does not certify the centered residual branch split, branch-resolved normalizer composition, basis bridge, terminal successor scalar residual identity, expression-level N38 provider, S37 division, shifted R43 closure, retained branch, or directed-rounded provider.",
    claim_boundary:
      h39TerminalSuccessorBranchAntisymmetricCommonNormalizerAttemptClaimBoundary(),
